mpact\": \"If both parts are populated, the outputs on PB0, PB1 and PB4 fight each other, the fan drive and tach readings become unreliable, and the ISP programmer sees two targets on the same bus.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist places two ATtiny microcontrollers (U2 and U4) on identical pin nets, including the PB0/PB1/PB4 fan-control lines and the ISP header. Unless this is an intentional either/or footprint, that is a contention problem. The remaining passives and connections look consistent with their stated roles, so confidence is moderate.\"\n}",
